          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "তুষার — tushār — \"snow; frost\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "শীতে উঁচু পাহাড়ে তুষার পড়ে। shīte ũchu pāhāṛe tushār pôṛe. In winter snow falls on the high mountains."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বরফ is ice, and snow in everyday talk; তুষার (tushār) is the careful word for snow and frost."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "তুষার (tushār) is Sanskrit tuṣāra, \"cold, frigid\", and as a noun \"frost, snow\" (Monier-Williams), taken over whole."
            }
          ]
        },
